Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:36:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] pushdown: EMERGENCE-Next N2, roots only from sites whose
 own roots reach k (opt-in)

pushdown.roots_from_k_sites_only (optional, absent = false = R0). Under the
shipped gate a site whose roots bucket is '<k' adds 1 root (bucket_lower), so
one event echoed to three sites reads as three independent roots. With N2 such
sites add none. Offline re-gate of the actual verdicts of the h1n+nd+N1 run at
seed 0: 0 of 22 true patterns lost, 5 of 9 supported conclusions on echo-decoy
keys dropped. Tests: R0 still sums single-root sites; N2 does not; a k-root
site still counts; N2 is a different pack hash.

Note: this code sat uncommitted (inactive: key absent) in this worktree while
the v2 ablation runs were executing; those runs are labelled dirty-tree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cc9kurj5azoGuhPNUVde8U
